ord for the 40th anniversary of the assassination, Gerald Posner examines all of the available evidence and reaches the only possible conclusion: Lee Harvey Oswald acted alone. There was no second gunman on the grassy knoll. The CIA was not involved. And although more than four million pages of documents have been released since Posner first made his case, they have served only to corroborate his findings. Case Closed remains the classic account against which all books about JFK's death must be measured.\"--BOOK JACKET.","publicationYear":1995,"displaySummary":"The CIA was not involved. And although more than four million pages of documents have been released since Posner first made his case, they have served only to corroborate his findings. Case Closed remains the classic account against which all books about JFK's death must be measured.\"--BOOK JACKET.","primaryTopic":"Crime, Policing & Violence","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"American History","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"American History","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"American History","mappedSubject":"American History","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily focuses on the assassination of JFK, a significant event in American history, while also addressing political implications surrounding the event, justifying the secondary classification.","id":"subject-evidence-book-case-closed-lee-harvey-oswald-and-the-assassination-of-jfk-gerald-posner-1"},{"source":"topic_classifier","rawLabel":"Crime, Policing & Violence","mappedSubject":"True Crime & Justice","score":2,"confidence":"low","note":"generated topic enrichment: embedding","id":"subject-evidence-book-case-closed-lee-harvey-oswald-and-the-assassination-of-jfk-gerald-posner-6"},{"source":"award_category","rawLabel":"Pulitzer Prize in History","mappedSubject":"History","score":1,"confidence":"low","sourceId":"source-award-record-pulitzer-hist